# BuildKit per-Dockerfile ignore file (deploy/Dockerfile → THIS file).
# Supported by any BuildKit-capable engine (Docker 23+ default, podman, buildah).
# It keeps the build context to exactly what the build reads — without it,
# `docker build -f deploy/Dockerfile .` would ship gigabytes of target/ to the daemon.
target/
.git/
.github/
docs/
installer/
deploy/
**/*.md
**/corpus/
crates/*/tests/
# fuzz/ is manifest-excluded (root Cargo.toml) — safe to skip.
# NOTE: cairn-x ITSELF must ship: it is a workspace member, and cargo
# refuses to load the workspace if a member's manifest is missing from
# the build context (the failure is "failed to load manifest for
# workspace member", not a missing-source error — easy to misread).
crates/cairn-x/fuzz/
crates/cairn-app/
